! Catppuccin Latte, as an X resource fragment.
!
! The same resource names Omarchy's own tk.Xresources publishes, so "dark"
! and "system" differ only in where the values came from -- see ui/xres.tcl.
! Loaded with `option readfile` at `interactive` priority, which outranks the
! root window's RESOURCE_MANAGER; that is the whole of "light/dark overrides
! system".
!
! Everything below the first block is an extension this UI needs and the
! stock Omarchy fragment does not publish yet (*mode and the named hues).
! Written in the shape it is being asked for upstream, so that when it does
! publish them, `system` picks them up through the identical code path and
! nothing here has to change.

! -- read by Tk 9's ttk `default` theme AND by classic widgets -------------
*background:                    #eff1f5
*foreground:                    #4c4f69
*activeBackground:              #d5d7df
*disabledForeground:            #9ea0af
*selectBackground:              #ccd0da
*selectForeground:              #4c4f69
*troughColor:                   #dbdee4
*windowColor:                   #e5e7ed

! -- classic widgets only (ttk never reads these) --------------------------
*activeForeground:              #4c4f69
*highlightBackground:           #eff1f5
*highlightColor:                #1e66f5
*insertBackground:              #4c4f69
*selectColor:                   #1e66f5

*Text.background:               #e5e7ed
*Entry.background:              #e5e7ed
*Listbox.background:            #e5e7ed
*Spinbox.background:            #e5e7ed

*Menu.activeBackground:         #ccd0da
*Menu.activeForeground:         #4c4f69
*Menu.borderWidth:              1

! -- the omarchy* extension contract (tk-omarchy-theme/docs/consuming.md) --
! Prefixed, not bare `*red`: these are not names Tk or Xt look up, and an
! unqualified one would be handed to every X client that has a resource of
! that name. Looked up under class Foreground.
*omarchyMode:                   light
*omarchyAccent:                 #1e66f5
*omarchyMuted:                  #acb0be
*omarchyRed:                    #d20f39
*omarchyGreen:                  #40a02b
*omarchyYellow:                 #df8e1d
*omarchyBlue:                   #1e66f5
*omarchyMagenta:                #ea76cb
*omarchyCyan:                   #179299
*omarchyOrange:                 #d84e2b
